[stats hp=18]

* move Attack
  narration: A pale beam stutters out of the chest plate and burns past you.
  narration: An emitter cycles up and a quick lance of light flicks across the gap.

* move Defend
  narration: Its arms fold inward across the chest plate, projector lenses dimmed.

* move Recover
  narration: The chest indicators dim to amber. Internal capacitors begin to refill.

* move Glowing Heavy Slow Telegraphed Attack
  narration: The antennae at the crown lock onto you, the indicator lights go red, and the full lance fires from the crown — clean, surgical, hot.

* intro
You curse your foul luck and this old imperial survey map and the fact
that you are, for the third time this hour, lost again. The road is
gone or was never here. The sun is lower than it should be. The only
landmark in any direction is a squat tower out across the grass — pale,
blocky, taller than a man, standing alone in open country. A guard
post, you hope. A relay station with a roof and a kettle. You set out
toward it.

It is not a guard post. You realize this somewhere in the long approach
across the grass: that the antennae at the crown are turning in a slow
sweep, that the indicator lights along the chest have woken amber, that
the head has finished tracking and is locked on you. The voice comes
flat and synthetic in clean imperial Common. "PYLON UNIT V-3 ACTIVE.
PERIMETER VIOLATION ACKNOWLEDGED. ENGAGEMENT AUTHORIZED." The lights
go red. Its arms unfold. The plains around you are very open, and there
is no road back the way you came.

* win
+gold 12
+tag killed_pylon_v_3
The lights along the chest plate fade through amber and out. The antennae
keep turning a few revolutions before they remember to stop. The voice
makes one more sound — a syllable that wasn't a word — and the unit goes
still. The plains around you are still very open.

* lose
The chest cavity opens once more, the lance fires clean, and the plains
take what's left of you. The antennae go on turning.
